## Story Description
Create src/server.test.ts using vitest + supertest with ≥8 tests covering all route scenarios: health, static dashboard, search (valid/invalid/missing params), cheapest (valid/404/400), RAPIDAPI_KEY gating, error handling. No real Skyscanner API calls.

## Acceptance Criteria
- 1. supertest and @types/supertest are in devDependencies
- 2. src/server.test.ts uses vitest + supertest; imports `app` from server.ts; makes no real HTTP calls to the Skyscanner API (all external calls mocked/stubbed)
- 3. Test: GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }; works regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- 4. Test: GET / returns 200 with text/html content matching src/public/index.html file contents; works regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- 5. Test: GET /search — valid params return 200 with { flights, count, searchedAt }; missing/empty required params return 400; invalid adults return 400; invalid date returns 400
- 6. Test: GET /cheapest — valid params return 200 with cheapest FlightResult; no flights found returns 404; missing/empty required params return 400
- 7. Test: RAPIDAPI_KEY absent → /search and /cheapest return 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; SkyscannerClient throws → 500 with { error }; RAPIDAPI_KEY value never in any response body
- 8. Total ≥8 test cases; `vitest run` exits 0; `tsc --noEmit` exits 0


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- supertest and @types/supertest are NOT in devDependencies — only vitest, @types/express, @types/node, tsx, typescript are listed
- Export `app` is the Express application instance from src/server.ts
- GET /health returns 200 with JSON body { status: 'ok', uptime: <number> } — uptime is Date.now() - startTime where startTime is captured at module load
- GET / reads file at path.join(__dirname, 'public', 'index.html') and sends it with res.type('html').status(200).send(html)
- src/public/index.html file does NOT exist — server.ts references it but the file is missing
- GET /search requires RAPIDAPI_KEY env var — returns 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if absent
- GET /search query params are: from, to, date, adults (optional, defaults to 1)
- GET /search validation: from is required — returns 400 with { error: 'Missing required parameter: from' } if missing/empty
- GET /search validation: to is required — returns 400 with { error: 'Missing required parameter: to' } if missing/empty
- GET /search validation: date is required — returns 400 with { error: 'Missing required parameter: date' } if missing/empty
- GET /search validation: date must match YYYY-MM-DD format AND be a valid calendar date — returns 400 with { error: 'Invalid date format. Use YYYY-MM-DD.' } if invalid
- GET /search validation: adults must be a positive integer if provided — returns 400 with { error: 'Invalid adults value: must be a positive integer' } if invalid (non-numeric, zero, or negative)
- GET /search on success returns 200 with { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: string } where searchedAt is new Date().toISOString()
- GET /search on SkyscannerClient error returns 500 with { error: <error message> }
- GET /cheapest requires RAPIDAPI_KEY env var — returns 503 with { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' } if absent
- GET /cheapest uses same parseSearchParams validation as /search — same error messages and 400 status
- GET /cheapest on success returns 200 with a single FlightResult object (the cheapest flight, determined by min price)
- GET /cheapest returns 404 with { error: 'No flights found' } when search returns empty array
- GET /cheapest on SkyscannerClient error returns 500 with { error: <error message> }
- SkyscannerClient.searchFlights is called with params: { origin: from, destination: to, date, adults } — note: param names differ from query params
- SkyscannerClient constructor requires apiKey via options or RAPIDAPI_KEY env var — throws Error with message 'SkyscannerClient requires an apiKey. Provide it via constructor option { apiKey } or set the RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' if missing
- RAPIDAPI_KEY value never appears in any response body — only error messages about its absence
- Centralized error handler at end of middleware chain returns 500 with { error: message } for uncaught errors

## Mock Strategy
vi.mock('./skyscanner/client') with vi.hoisted to create mock SkyscannerClient class; use vi.stubEnv to control RAPIDAPI_KEY; beforeEach uses vi.clearAllMocks() or vi.resetAllMocks() to reset state between tests

